import re
p='work/ORANGE-L5-en-GB/b01.txt'; t=open(p).read()
U='For UK readers: '
NOTES={1: 'VAT-registered businesses must charge VAT on most sales, registration becomes compulsory once turnover passes the threshold, and selling to customers in the EU since Brexit can create separate VAT obligations there, so check with an accountant.', 2: 'VAT is usually due when an advance payment is received rather than when the service is delivered, while Corporation Tax generally follows accounts prepared under UK accounting standards, which recognise prepaid income as it is earned, so check the timing with an accountant.', 3: 'marketing and advertising costs are generally deductible for Corporation Tax or Income Tax if they are incurred wholly and exclusively for the trade, although client entertaining is not, so check with an accountant.', 4: 'estate agents must give buyers material information about a property under consumer protection law, and the Equality Act 2010 prohibits discrimination when letting or selling homes, so check advertising wording with a solicitor or Trading Standards guidance.', 5: 'inviting people to invest is a financial promotion that generally must be made or approved by a firm authorised by the Financial Conduct Authority unless an exemption applies, so take advice before you publicise an offering.', 6: 'in an asset purchase, employees may transfer to the buyer automatically under the TUPE regulations, and asset and share deals are taxed very differently, so a solicitor and an accountant should review the structure.', 7: 'Capital Gains Tax is usually charged on the whole gain in the tax year of sale even when the price is paid in instalments, although HMRC may let the tax be paid in instalments where payments stretch over a long period, so check with an accountant.', 8: 'workers paid mainly by commission must still receive at least the National Minimum Wage averaged over the pay period, and holiday pay may need to include regular commission, so check your plan with an employment adviser.', 9: 'self-employed commercial agents selling goods may be entitled to compensation or an indemnity when the agency ends under the Commercial Agents Regulations 1993, while distributors generally are not, so a solicitor should review the agreement.', 10: 'under UK accounting standards an internally built brand is generally not shown on the balance sheet, while a purchased brand is recognised and usually amortised, and registering the trade mark with the UK Intellectual Property Office strengthens protection.', 11: "the Competition and Markets Authority has examined 'shrinkflation', and retailers must generally display unit prices so shoppers can compare value, so make pack size changes clear.", 12: 'marketing and advertising spending is generally deductible for Corporation Tax if incurred wholly and exclusively for the trade, so the net cost depends on the business remaining profitable; check the details with an accountant.', 13: 'there is no general UK law against high prices, but the Competition and Markets Authority can act against unfair commercial practices and against dominant firms that abuse their position, so take advice before sharp emergency price rises.', 14: 'selling into the UK can require UKCA or CE marking for some products, compliance with UK GDPR, and consumer rights such as a 14-day cancellation period for most online sales, so check the rules for your product.', 15: 'for companies, foreign exchange gains and losses on trading transactions are usually taxed as part of trading profits, with special rules for loans and derivatives, so check the treatment with an accountant.', 16: 'resale price maintenance is generally prohibited under the Competition Act 1998, so a supplier can recommend but not usually fix the price a retailer charges; check distribution terms with a competition lawyer.', 17: 'new rules on subscription contracts under the Digital Markets, Competition and Consumers Act 2024 require clear pre-contract information, reminders and an easy way to cancel, so check which provisions are already in force.', 18: 'invoice finance providers often set concentration limits on any single debtor, and bans on assigning receivables in many business contracts are ineffective under the 2018 assignment of receivables regulations, so ask your lender how this affects your facility.', 19: 'under UK accounting standards most content and advertising costs are expensed as incurred, though some website development costs may be capitalised, so ask an accountant how your spending will be treated.', 20: "the CAP Code enforced by the Advertising Standards Authority requires paid or gifted posts to be clearly identified as advertising, for example with '#ad', and fake reviews are banned under consumer law, so label endorsements clearly.", 21: "UK GDPR and the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations generally require consent for marketing emails to individuals and for non-essential cookies, so check your practices against guidance from the Information Commissioner's Office.", 22: 'agreements between competitors can breach the Competition Act 1998 if they restrict competition, and the Competition and Markets Authority publishes guidance on joint ventures and co-operation, so take advice before sharing prices or markets.', 23: 'the UK has no franchise-specific law or mandatory disclosure document, although the British Franchise Association sets a voluntary code of ethics and general contract and consumer law still apply, so ask a franchise solicitor to review the agreement.', 24: 'a share sale may qualify for Business Asset Disposal Relief if conditions are met, while an asset sale can create a double tax charge for a company and its owners, so check the structure with an accountant early.', 25: 'the right to receive an earnout can itself be treated as an asset for Capital Gains Tax, and earnouts paid in shares or loan notes have special rules, so take tax advice before agreeing the terms.', 26: 'investment gold is generally exempt from VAT, and dealers in precious metals may have duties under the Money Laundering Regulations, so check what applies before you market these products.', 27: 'firms giving financial advice must be authorised by the Financial Conduct Authority and follow its suitability rules and the Consumer Duty, so check any adviser or partner on the FCA register.', 28: 'invoice finance is widely available, and the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998 lets businesses claim statutory interest and compensation on late payments, so plan cash for long payment terms.', 29: 'credit reference agencies and accounts filed at Companies House are common sources for checking a business customer, and personal credit data is protected under UK GDPR, so use credit information within those rules.', 30: "public bodies buy under the Procurement Act 2023, with opportunities advertised on the government's central digital platform and Contracts Finder, so register there and read each tender's requirements carefully.", 32: 'VAT is generally charged on the discounted price, and business gifts above a modest annual value per person can create a VAT charge, so check promotions with an accountant.', 33: 'businesses must register for VAT once taxable turnover passes the registration threshold, and selling to EU consumers may require registering under the EU One Stop Shop, so check current thresholds and rules with HMRC guidance or an accountant.', 34: 'in England and Wales an apology does not in itself amount to an admission of negligence under the Compensation Act 2006, and Scotland has its own Apologies Act, but statements should still be reviewed by a solicitor.', 36: 'referral rewards and affiliate links must be disclosed under the CAP Code, and claims about income or results must be backed by evidence, so check community marketing against ASA guidance.', 37: 'since Brexit the EU geo-blocking rules no longer apply in Great Britain, so businesses can usually charge different prices in different countries, but price displays must still be clear and not misleading.', 38: 'food labelling, including allergen information, is regulated and enforced with guidance from the Food Standards Agency, and pet food has its own rules, so check labels with Trading Standards or a specialist.', 40: 'goods imported into the UK pay duty under the UK Global Tariff, and lower rates may apply under trade agreements if rules of origin are met, so check classification and origin before you place an order.', 41: "pooling investors' money in property can be a collective investment scheme that only FCA-authorised firms may operate or promote, so take legal advice before marketing a property investment.", 42: "consumer law bans misleading practices, including hidden 'drip' pricing, and pre-ticked boxes cannot be used to add extra paid items, so make every add-on a clear, active choice.", 43: 'companies pay Corporation Tax on profits, with a lower rate for smaller profits, and marketing costs are generally deductible, so compare options after tax with an accountant.', 45: 'VAT, Making Tax Digital requirements and any overseas tax registrations should be part of the plan, so ask an accountant to review the structure before launch.', 46: "self-employed people pay Income Tax through Self Assessment, often with payments on account towards the next year's bill, so plan for a higher bill after a strong year.", 49: 'price-fixing between competitors is prohibited under the Competition Act 1998, and a dominant business can break the law by pricing below cost to force out rivals, so take advice from a competition lawyer.'}
parts=re.split(r'(?m)^(?====== )',t); out=[]; k=0
for ch in parts:
    m=re.match(r'===== \S+-(\d{3})',ch)
    if m and int(m.group(1)) in NOTES:
        n=int(m.group(1)); a=ch.index('## Core Content'); b=ch.index('\n## ',a+5)
        paras=ch[a:b].split('\n\n')
        i=next((k2 for k2,x in enumerate(paras) if 'REGION-SPECIFIC RULE' in x),len(paras)-1)
        if i==0: i=len(paras)-1
        paras[i]=paras[i].rstrip()+' '+U+NOTES[n]; k+=1
        ch=ch[:a]+'\n\n'.join(paras)+ch[b:]
    out.append(ch)
open(p,'w').write(''.join(out)); print('ok',k,len(NOTES))
